# Repo-root Docker build context filter. All four app images
# (apps/{api,web,h5,bot}/Dockerfile) build from the monorepo root with `COPY . .`,
# so anything not excluded here is shipped to the daemon and lands in the build-stage
# image layers + cache. Keep this in sync with .gitignore.
#
# Why this matters:
#  - Build speed: node_modules/.git/.turbo/.next are large and useless — pnpm
#    reinstalls from the lockfile inside the container anyway, and each app rebuilds
#    its own dist/.next fresh in the build stage.
#  - Secrets: a physical `.env` (gitignored but present locally, holding real
#    OTP_SECRET / BETTER_AUTH_SECRET) must never reach a build layer or cache.

# Dependencies — reinstalled from the lockfile in-container
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — regenerated in the build stage
**/dist
dist-worker
**/dist-worker
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling caches
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets & local env — never ship into a layer; keep the checked-in examples.
# Both root and `**/` forms: unanchored patterns only match the context root, so
# without `**/` a physical `apps/{api,bot}/.env` would still land in a build layer.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.deploy.example
!.env.free.example
!**/.env.example

# Runtime / local artifacts
.uploads
.git
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode

# The images don't need these; they only bloat the context
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
